## Build.ROM   [-e]## Steven Glass# November 16, 1988## This script builds the toolbox portion of the ROM.  Its easy to use# and fun too.## Just have your directory set to the folder that this script is in and# type BUILD.ROM.## If you want to force the entire rom to be re assembled, just pass# the -e option:  BUILD.ROM -e.## What files do you need to build the ROM?  Well you need all the files# in the project GSToolbox.  To get these files you could use the following# commands:##     MountProject fettuccine:gsprojects:gstoolbox#     CheckOutDir -project gstoolbox work:gstoolbox -r#     CheckOut -a -r -project gstoolbox## The -a option could be replaced with a -newer if you already have sources# on your disk and you only want the latest.##     CheckOut -newer -r -project gstoolbox#############################################################################directory romBuildProgram {parameters} ROM.LOAD